--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
libvips (via the sharp image library)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Licence: LGPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream: https://github.com/libvips/libvips

`packages/image-utils` depends on `sharp` (Apache-2.0), which installs a prebuilt libvips binary as
`@img/sharp-libvips-linux-x64` (and the musl variant). That binary is LGPL-3.0-or-later and is
present in the published application container image. libvips is used as a shared library through
sharp's own bindings; it is not modified here. Source for the exact version is available from the
upstream project and from the npm package, and sharp can be rebuilt against a system libvips.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
System packages in the container images
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

`deploy/docker/app.Dockerfile` installs the following Debian packages into the application image:

  ffmpeg, fontconfig, fonts-dejavu-core, fonts-comic-neue, tini, ca-certificates

`services/kokoro/Dockerfile` installs:

  espeak-ng, libsndfile1

Each remains under its own licence, which is unchanged by inclusion in these images. Two are
copyleft and worth naming: Debian's `ffmpeg` build is distributed under the GNU GPL (OpenManga
invokes it as a separate executable for video and audio export; it is not linked into OpenManga's
own code), and `espeak-ng` is GPL-3.0-or-later (used by the Kokoro service for phonemisation). The
licence text for every installed package is present in `/usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright` inside
the image. The base images — `oven/bun`, `nginx:alpine`, `postgres:alpine`, `redis:alpine` — carry
their own notices.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Other dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The remaining runtime dependencies are under permissive licences that require only that their own
copyright notices and licence text be preserved, which happens through the package metadata in
`node_modules`: MIT, ISC, BSD-3-Clause, 0BSD, Apache-2.0 and Unlicense. The Apache-2.0 ones include
`drizzle-orm`, `sharp` and `detect-libc`; `postgres` is released under the Unlicense.

Two build-time-only dependencies are not in that set, and neither ends up in a published image:

  - `lightningcss` (MPL-2.0), pulled in by Tailwind CSS v4's Vite plugin. Used unmodified; only its
    CSS output ships.
  - `caniuse-lite` (CC-BY-4.0), pulled in by browserslist. Its data is used unmodified at build time.
    Attribution: https://caniuse.com, by Alexis Deveria and contributors.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Generated output
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Artwork, narration audio and exports produced by a running OpenManga instance come from the AI
providers the operator configures with their own keys, plus local Kokoro synthesis. Rights in that
output are governed by the terms of whichever provider generated it. OpenManga claims nothing in it.
